                            <div class="card"><div class="card-header bg-white border-0"><div class="collapsible-link" data-target="#collapse2"><span><strong>Q2:</strong> How does the eBook writing process work in Melbourne?</span></div></div><div id="collapse2" class="collapse"><div class="card-body text"><p>It starts with a detailed briefing, a conversation about your eBook concept, your target audience, your goals, and what you want the finished book to accomplish. Your writer then develops a full chapter outline for your approval before writing begins. The manuscript is written in stages, with drafts shared in batches so you can give feedback and request changes before we move forward. Nothing is finalised without your approval at every stage. The whole process is genuinely collaborative, you’re shaping the eBook as it develops, not waiting months to see a finished draft you’ve had no input on.</p></div></div></div>
                            <div class="card"><div class="card-header bg-white border-0"><div class="collapsible-link" data-target="#collapse3"><span><strong>Q3:</strong> How much do eBook writing services cost in Melbourne?</span></div></div><div id="collapse3" class="collapse"><div class="card-body text"><p>eBook writing costs in Melbourne vary depending on the length, category, and complexity of the project. A shorter business eBook based on existing material costs less than a full-length fiction manuscript or a research-heavy instructional guide. Most professional eBook writing services charge per word or per project, with rates reflecting the writer’s experience and the scope of work involved. We don’t publish fixed rates because they rarely reflect what a specific project actually needs. Get in touch with your concept and we’ll give you a clear, honest quote built around your eBook specifically.</p></div></div></div>
                            <div class="card"><div class="card-header bg-white border-0"><div class="collapsible-link" data-target="#collapse4"><span><strong>Q4:</strong> How long does it take to write an eBook in Melbourne?</span></div></div><div id="collapse4" class="collapse"><div class="card-body text"><p>A standard eBook of around 20,000 to 40,000 words typically takes four to eight weeks from briefing to final delivery, accounting for outlining, chapter drafting, and revision rounds. Shorter eBooks, lead magnets, focused guides, can be completed faster. Longer or more complex projects, full-length fiction, heavily researched non-fiction, multi-chapter instructional content, take longer. We’ll give you a realistic timeline at the start of your project based on your specific eBook and publishing goals, and we communicate clearly if anything changes along the way.</p></div></div></div>
                            <div class="card"><div class="card-header bg-white border-0"><div class="collapsible-link" data-target="#collapse5"><span><strong>Q5:</strong> Do I own the rights to my eBook after it is written?</span></div></div><div id="collapse5" class="collapse"><div class="card-body text"><p>Yes, completely and from the very beginning. Everything produced belongs entirely to you, the manuscript, the content, and the finished eBook, including publishing rights, adaptation rights, and all future royalties. Our writers work under a confidentiality agreement and have no claim over the work they produce for you. Your name goes on the cover, and the eBook is yours in every legal and creative sense. We retain no rights, credit, or ongoing interest in the work after delivery.</p></div></div></div>
                            <div class="card"><div class="card-header bg-white border-0"><div class="collapsible-link" data-target="#collapse6"><span><strong>Q6:</strong> Can an eBook writer turn my idea into a complete book?</span></div></div><div id="collapse6" class="collapse"><div class="card-body text"><p>Absolutely, and that’s exactly what professional eBook writing services are built for. You don’t need a finished outline or a fully developed concept before getting in touch. Some clients come with detailed chapter plans, existing blog posts, and research already organised. Others come with nothing more than a topic and a rough sense of what they want to say. We work with both, using the briefing and outlining process to develop your idea into a well-structured, complete eBook before writing begins. If you have an idea worth turning into an eBook, we can help you get it there.</p></div></div></div>
